Mount the sensor facing forward on the servo horn. Ensure it can turn without hitting the chassis or pulling the wires.
Step 5 — Connect the servo motor
The servo normally has three wires:
Servo wire	Connection
Signal, often orange/yellow	Arduino D3
Power, usually red	Regulated 5V supply suitable for the servo
Ground, usually brown/black	Common GND
Wire colours can vary, so check the servo labels.
For a reliable competition robot, use a suitable regulated supply for the servo rather than relying on the Arduino's 5V output under load. Connect the servo supply ground to Arduino GND. 

